  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_MINERALNUTRITION_DIAGRAM_Q01 - Hydroponics nutrient solution culture set-up</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The diagram below shows a typical laboratory set-up for nutrient solution culture (hydroponics). Identify the component labelled <strong>X</strong> and its primary function.</p><p><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 280" width="360" height="280"><rect x="10" y="10" width="340" height="260" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#cccccc" stroke-width="1"/><rect x="110" y="120" width="140" height="130" rx="6" fill="#d9efe2" stroke="#2d5a3f" stroke-width="2"/><line x1="110" y1="140" x2="250" y2="140" stroke="#4a8c66" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4,3"/><rect x="168" y="110" width="24" height="16" fill="#e6e6e6" stroke="#666666" stroke-width="1"/><line x1="180" y1="50" x2="180" y2="145" stroke="#3b7a3b" stroke-width="4"/><path d="M180,85 Q150,70 140,85 Q155,95 180,85" fill="#6ab04c" stroke="#3b7a3b" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M180,70 Q210,55 220,70 Q205,80 180,70" fill="#6ab04c" stroke="#3b7a3b" stroke-width="1.5"/><path d="M180,145 C170,170 150,190 145,220 M180,145 C180,175 178,205 180,235 M180,145 C195,170 210,195 215,225" fill="none" stroke="#7a5c3e" stroke-width="1.5"/><polygon points="118,65 138,65 132,165 124,165" fill="#cce5ff" stroke="#336699" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="205" y1="230" x2="275" y2="95" stroke="#d9534f" stroke-width="4"/><path d="M275,95 L295,85 L305,100" fill="none" stroke="#d9534f" stroke-width="4"/><rect x="198" y="225" width="12" height="16" fill="#e08e45" stroke="#8a4b16" stroke-width="1"/><text x="155" y="102" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#222222">Cotton</text><text x="20" y="95" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#222222">Funnel for</text><text x="20" y="108" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#222222">water &amp; nutrients</text><text x="285" y="125" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#b32400">X</text><line x1="282" y1="120" x2="262" y2="120" stroke="#b32400" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="260" y="210" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#222222">Nutrient</text><text x="260" y="223" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#222222">solution</text></svg></p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Step 1: Diagram Interpretation</strong><br/>The schematic represents a hydroponic culture apparatus in which a plant is supported at the neck of a container by cotton, with its roots immersed in a defined mineral nutrient solution. A funnel on the left allows addition of purified water and nutrient salts, while the tube dipping into the bottom of the solution (labelled <strong>X</strong>) is connected to an external air supply.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Conceptual Principle</strong><br/>In hydroponics, nutrient solutions must be adequately aerated to obtain optimum plant growth because roots require oxygen for aerobic respiration, which supplies ATP for active mineral absorption into the symplast.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Final Conclusion</strong><br/>The structure labelled <strong>X</strong> is the aerating tube, and its primary function is to supply oxygen to the roots for respiration and active mineral uptake.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Aerating tube; supplies oxygen to the roots for respiration and active mineral uptake.</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Funnel; used for adding purified water and mineral nutrient salts.</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Cotton plug; prevents all gaseous exchange around the stem.</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Xylem vessel; transports mineral salts upward to the shoot.</p>]]></text></answer>
